/**
 * LUNG CANCER: registry-only trial records, part 2 of 2. Every interventional phase 2, 1/2, 2/3 or 3 trial on
 * ClinicalTrials.gov that on 2026-09-25 was recruiting, not yet recruiting or enrolling by invitation (plus the
 * phase 3 and 2/3 trials that are active but closed to recruitment), names lung cancer, non-small-cell lung cancer
 * or small-cell lung cancer in its title or conditions, and was not already in the corpus. Generated from the v2 API
 * snapshot cached under /tmp/lung by the lung deep dive (the generator is /tmp/lung/gen-registry.py, adapted from
 * the colorectal one); registry facts only, no outcomes. Trials with results, and the trials that set the standard
 * of care, are hand-written in ./lung-treatment-trials*.ts. UK sites are quoted in `notes`. Linked from the glossary
 * term `lung-trials-open-today` so none is an orphan. Records link to the subtype page the registry text names
 * (small-cell by stage, the driver-mutation pages, resectable and stage III non-small-cell, the histologies) and to
 * `lung-cancer` itself only when it names none, so the cancer page stays under its markup ceiling
 * (src/app/record-fold.test.ts). Mesothelioma, thymic tumours and trials whose only lung involvement is a metastasis
 * from another primary are left out.
 */
